.TH "PKGSOURCE_YAML" "3" "" "libpkgsource\-yaml 1.1.0" "libpkgsource\-yaml"
.SH NAME
pkgsource_yaml \- parse strict native YAML into libpkgsource declarations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include <libpkgsource\-yaml/libpkgsource\-yaml.h>

std::vector<pkgsource::profile_declaration>
pkgsource::yaml::parse_profiles_yaml(
    std::string_view bytes,
    pkgsource::source_origin origin,
    const pkgsource::yaml::parse_limits& limits = {});

pkgsource::recipe_declaration
pkgsource::yaml::parse_recipe_yaml(
    std::string_view bytes,
    pkgsource::source_origin origin,
    const pkgsource::yaml::parse_limits& limits = {});
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[CR]libpkgsource\-yaml\f[R] parses one caller\-owned in\-memory YAML document into parser\-neutral \f[CR]libpkgsource\f[R] declarations.
It never opens paths or invokes \f[CR]profile_catalog::seal()\f[R] or \f[CR]seal_source()\f[R].
.PP
The profile parser accepts \f[CR]zeppe\-lin.profiles/1\f[R].
The recipe parser accepts \f[CR]zeppe\-lin.recipe/1\f[R], including its optional check program.
Protocol versions are document fields, not C++ entry\-point generations.
.SH STRICTNESS
The parser rejects multiple or empty documents, directives, duplicate and unknown keys, non\-scalar mapping keys, anchors, aliases, merge keys, custom or kind\-incompatible tags, scalar requirement shorthand, and protocol/type drift.
.SH LIMITS
\f[CR]parse_limits\f[R] bounds total document bytes, bytes in one scalar, retained nodes, and nesting depth.
The root is depth one.
All ceilings are inclusive.
Exceeding one throws \f[CR]yaml_error\f[R] with code \f[CR]resource_limit\f[R].
.SH ERRORS
Syntax, unsupported\-feature, schema, value, and resource failures throw \f[CR]yaml_error\f[R].
The value retains a stable \f[CR]yaml_error_code\f[R], caller\-supplied document label, protocol path, and one\-based line and column.
.PP
A failure raised while constructing one core semantic value is translated to \f[CR]invalid_value\f[R] at its YAML location.
Later failures from profile or source sealing remain \f[CR]pkgsource::error\f[R] and are not translated.
.SH PROVIDER
Only the private libyaml event provider knows libyaml types.
Grammar behavior, diagnostics, and public ABI remain provider\-neutral.
.SH AUTHORITY
Parsed declarations are not package\-source authority.
Callers explicitly pass profile declarations to \f[CR]profile_catalog::seal()\f[R] and recipe declarations to \f[CR]seal_source()\f[R].
Aggregation, precedence, semantic normalization, identity, resolution, fetching, execution, planning, and storage remain outside this library.
.SH ABI
The first public ABI is \f[CR]libpkgsource\-yaml.so.1\f[R].
Public headers expose no libyaml types.
The library requires \f[CR]libpkgsource\f[R] major API 3 and keeps libyaml private in pkg\-config metadata.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]pkgsource_profiles_yaml(5)\f[R], \f[CR]pkgsource_recipe_yaml(5)\f[R]
